  {
    "episode_id": 76735,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/7/6/76735.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 4,
    "turn_text": "It is the honor of my life to fight alongside each and every one of you. We will save America. It's Choose Your Fighter Time, sending the fire brains. Welcome back to Firebrand. We are broadcasting live from the Rumble Studios here in the United States Capitol in Washington, DC. I've got a terrific guest who's going to join me in a moment. Jeremy Carl, he is a commentator. He is a scholar at the Claremont Institute where we get so many of our ideas. Really, it's the group that's filling the intellectual vacuum that's been abandoned by so many of the compromised think tanks in this town. But before we get to his work critiquing DEI and the left's current incarnation of multiculturalism and the exclusion of a pretty substantial portion of the country, Jeremy, I've got to talk to you about just what has the capital abuzz right now. You've seen Pelosi offer something other than a full-throated endorsement of Joe Biden. Joe Biden has scurried off to the Congressional Black Caucus where he is being protected by the likes of Frederica Wilson and Maxine Waters. Those are the stalwarts, the Congresswoman Beatty. You've seen Emmanuel Cleaver out there advocating for him. But then people like Richard Torres, a Democrat from New York, people like Michael Bennett who went on CNN last night and just Full-aid Joe Biden it is all over the place. So I'm I'm two in it. I'm in the committees with these people I'm seeing the funeral like look on their face What is your perspective on this moment in presidential political history that we are in?",
    "speaker_id": "SPEAKER_05",
    "inferred_speaker_name": null,
    "inferred_speaker_role": null,
