    "turn_idx": 43,
    "turn_text": "Sure. So we are a public policy think tank, but we're a little bit different. You alluded to that in some of your earlier is we're less kind of like writing white papers on what marginal tax rates should be and more about trying to educate people about our founding principles and attempting to restore our founding principles to kind of a governing role in society, which we would argue that for some time they've essentially been displaced. So that's the kind of central principle thing. So it actually sort of tends to be a kind of very high-minded and elevated and philosophical conversation. And in fact, I've kind of been very grubby in this book in kind of getting into a very messy area of public policy. But I think it's actually one that really does implicate some of these fundamental founding questions about unalienable rights and equality and things that are promised to us in the Declaration and Constitution.",
