    "episode_id": 76735,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/7/6/76735.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 117,
    "turn_text": "Well, I think that you already are beginning to see little bits of this, a friend of mine named Nate Fisher has a group new founding and again, it's not sort of doing anything explicitly on race, but I think it kind of indirectly touches on a lot of this for kind of people are getting pushed out of the system, whether it be because of their ethnic background or because of their religious values or whatever else. And there's real market inefficiencies to exploit there. I think you're also gonna see, and again, this could have some weird backfires. You're gonna see more young white people becoming entrepreneurs because they realize there's no place for them as easily in the system. So they're gonna go outside the system. And you're already seeing this. Again, I talked to a lot of younger white people. First big show I did on this book was with Charlie Kirk. And Charlie said, you know, hey, when I talked to my donors about this type of issue, they're like, You know, they get a little bit nervous. They're like, you know, can you say that? It sort of sounds racist. Not all of them be said, but some of the older guys that they do. When I said, when I go on a college campus and I talk to young white people, they say, this is the number one issue we're facing. Thank you so much for raising it. So I think there's a generational change at foot. And it's going to develop in some interesting and unpredictable ways.",
