    "turn_text": "Right, so it was actually a perfect illustration of my thesis, right? Like, put on the Klan hood now, Jeremy, because he said it's OK to be white. But I think I actually really like, I mean, we've done a great job of stigmatizing the word DEI, and I think that's great. I have no objection to us using it. But I also think it's very important that we kind of take the battle now to a new front, and we don't mystify what DEI means, which is DEI. I mean, there's more at stake, but it's core. It's about anti-whiteness. And it is about the opposite of Merit. And it's not just for folks in your district. I mean, I live in a rural area outside of small city in Montana. So I sort of have friends who are dealing with the same thing. It's not just for big companies, it's everywhere that you're going to be at a disadvantage from this. And as the demographics of America change, that is going to actually get even worse for you unless we do something to stop it.",
